Applied the `[profile]` extra's GenericSetup profile with `@pytest.mark.portal(profiles=[...])` rather than a `portal` fixture that shadowed pytest-plone's and called `applyProfile` by hand. Each test module now declares the profile it needs at the top, so a plain site is the default and a module that never asks for the extra gets one — which is how `test_not_installed` stops needing a second fixture to opt back out. The tests run as a site manager, granted before the marker rather than through its own `roles` argument: the marker grants roles after it applies profiles, which is too late for an import step that creates content. @ericof
